iness\nLifelong learning\nLogin\nLogin\nLogin\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\nSearch\nLanguage\nChoose language\nGerman\nEnglish\nDepartment of Computer Science\nDepartmentDepartment\nDepartmentOverview\nHistoryHistory\nWilhelm SchickardOverview\nWilhelm Schickard\nSchickards Rechenmaschine\nFestakt \"400 Jahre Rechenmaschine\"\nPublic collection\nHead & Committees\nStaff\nTechnical SupportTechnical Support\nTechnical SupportOverview\nForms\nStudentsStudents\nBesch\u00e4ftigteBesch\u00e4ftigte\nLibraryLibrary\nLibraryOverview\nLibrary CollectionLibrary Collection\nLoan Service\nFast delivery services\nOpen Access\nAnschaffungsvorschlag\nHow to find us\nNews\nStudiesStudies\nStudiesOverview\nProspective Students\nStudy StartStudy Start\nInformation for first-year studentsOverview\nInformation for first-year students\nMathematics Preparatory Course\nOnline Mathematics Bridging Course OMB+\nPreparatory Course Informatics for Life Scientists\nOffers for Prospective Students\nStudentsStudents\nStudentsOverview\nContactsContacts\nTeaching & Study OrganizationTeaching & Study Organization\nDownloadsDownloads\nInternationalInternational\nPractice & Profession\nFAQ\nResearch\nResearch Groups\nHow to find us\nFaculty of Science\nDepartment of Computer Science\nYou are here:\nHomeHome\nFacultiesFaculties\nFaculty of ScienceFaculty of Science\nDepartmentsDepartments\nComputer ScienceComputer Science\nDepartmentDepartment\nbackwards\nscroll forward\nWelcome to the Department of Computer Science!\nHead & Committees\nResearch Groups\nStaff\nWilhelm Schickard ushered in the era of computing devices in T\u00fcbingen \u2013 and never has computer science been as exciting as today, almost 400 years later. The more than 40 groups of the Wilhelm-Schickard Institute (WSI) teach, research and apply computer science at top level.\nThe research focus of the institute lies in the core areas of computer science as well as in bioinformatics, media informatics and cognitive science. T\u00fcbingen's computer scientists benefit from the diverse research environment within and outside the University of T\u00fcbingen.\nThe focus on machine learning is currently being rapidly expanded, in particular through the Cluster of Excellence \"Machine Learning in Science\" and the Baden-W\u00fcrttemberg Cyber Valley Initiative, which also includes the Max Planck Institute for Intelligent Systems and the University of Stuttgart. Together with these strong partners, the Department of Computer Science forms one of the centres for machine learning in Germany and Europe.\nThe study of computer science in T\u00fcbingen is correspondingly versatile and at the pulse of time: Join us in studying this young science in our Bachelor's and Master's programmes and become part of the success story!\nFacts & Numbers\nabout\n2000\nstudents\nin\n19\nstudy programs\ncurrently\n44\nresearch groups\nthird-party funded with\n12\nM \u20ac in 2021\n<\n>\nShare\nShare on Facebook (opens in new window)\nShare on LinkedIn (opens in new window)\nShare on Mastodon (opens in new window)\nShare on Bluesky (opens in new window)\nShare via email (opens in new window)\nHead of Department\nProf. Dr. Volker Franz\nHead of Department\nContact\nAdmission and studies\nCurrent Issues\nTalk announcements on\ntalks.tue.ai\n07.09.2026\nJob advertisement: Two Full Professors (W3) of Machine Learning & Intelligent Systems\nApplication deadline: 15.11.2026\nRead more\n15.12.2025\nERC Consolidator Grant for Andreas Geiger\nProf. Andreas Geiger's AI research will receive \u20ac2 million in funding from the EU over the next five\u2026\nRead more\n23.05.2025\nHuge success with the Excellence Strategy\nAll three clusters of excellence involving the Department of Computer Science will receive further\u2026\nRead more\nPrevious\n1\n2\n3\n4\n5\nNext\nShare\nShare on Facebook (opens in new window)\nShare on LinkedIn (opens in new window)\nShare on Mastodon (opens in new window)\nShare on Bluesky (opens in new window)\nShare via email (opens in new window)\nContact us\nUniversity of T\u00fcbingen\nGeschwister-Scholl-Platz\n72074 T\u00fcbingen Germany\nPhone: +49 7071 29-0\nContact us\nKey services\nOfficial bulletinsDisabled accessAdvice for international studentsMediaSemester DatesJobsOrganizing Your StudiesUniversity LibraryPrograms availableWelcome Center for Scholars\nFurther services\nSystem statusCorporate DesignConference materialsMapsCafeteria menuNewsletter Uni T\u00fcbingen aktuellStudent AdministrationStudium GeneraleUni A - ZUni shopCalendar of events\nPortals\nALMAExchange Mail (OWA)Research information system FITILIAS, moodleSearch for persons at the University (EPV)PraxisportalTimms Video PortalWebmail Uni T\u00fcbingen\nImprint\nData Privacy Statement\nBarrierefreiheit\nLeichte Sprache\nGeb\u00e4rdensprache\nRSS-Feed\nShortcut\nPrint\n\u00a9\n2026\nEberhard Karls Universit\u00e4t T\u00fcbingen", "links": [["Skip to main navigation", "https://uni-tuebingen.de/en/faculties/faculty-of-science/departments/computer-science/department/#ut-identifier--main-nav"], ["Skip to content", "https://uni-tuebingen.de/en/faculties/faculty-of-science/departments/computer-science/department/#ut-identifier--main-content"], ["Skip to footer", "https://uni-tuebingen.de/en/faculties/faculty-of-science/departments/computer-science/department/#ut-identifier--footer"], ["Skip to search", "https://uni-tuebingen.de/en/faculties/faculty-of-science/departments/computer-science/department/#ut-identifier--search-toggle"], ["", "https://uni-tuebingen.de/en/"], ["German", "https://uni-tuebingen.de/fakultaeten/mathematisch-naturwissenschaftliche-fakultaet/fachbereiche/informatik/fachbereich/"], ["English", "https://uni-tuebingen.de/en/faculties/faculty-of-science/departments/computer-science/department/"], ["Prospective Students", "https://uni-tuebingen.de/en/study/prospective-students/"], ["Current Students", "https://uni-tuebingen.de/en/study/"], ["Staff", "https://uni-tuebingen.de/en/staff/"], ["Teaching St